<body><main><header><a href="../../index.html">← ONE · The Last App</a><a href="../../../index.html">TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY</a></header>
<p class="tag">ONE · LIVING LIBRARY / AUTHOR WORKSPACE</p><h1>Helplessness &amp; Barnabas</h1><p>The Good Samaritan — newly labeled by Nathan Tabor</p>
<section class="panel"><div class="tag">AUTHOR'S CENTRAL THESIS — ORIGINAL WORDING</div><p class="statement">without barnabus there is NO paul</p><p>Central creative analogy: internal effort and voice belong to the individual; a Barnabas can become the second hand, second foot, advocate or external partner when someone has no traction.</p></section>
<div class="grid"><section class="box"><h2>ONE</h2><p>One voice. One personal experience. Inner struggle, calling and effort.</p><p class="muted">Authored analogy—not a literal anatomical proof of social dependency.</p></section><section class="box"><h2>TWO</h2><p>Two hands, two feet, two eyes: cooperation, balance, shared work and help.</p><p class="muted">Body anatomy has important exceptions; the symbolism is literary and theological.</p></section><section class="box"><h2>BARNABAS</h2><p>Advocacy in Acts 9:26–27. Seeking Saul and bringing him to Antioch in Acts 11:25–26.</p><p class="muted">Barnabas is NOT named as the literal Samaritan of Luke 10; this title is the author's interpretation.</p></section></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>Author's working space</h2><p>Write freely. Notes remain on this device/browser profile; they are not uploaded to the public GitHub repository. Export frequently to preserve your original work.</p><label for="draft">Draft material — your words</label><textarea id="draft" placeholder="Write a chapter, passage, instruction, or intervention…"></textarea><div class="row"><button id="save">Save on this device</button><button id="export" class="secondary">Export original text (.md)</button><button id="clear" class="secondary">Clear draft editor</button></div><p id="status" role="status" class="muted">Private draft is not synchronized or encrypted.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Connections for the complete work</h2><p><strong>Luke 10:25–37:</strong> the Samaritan stops and supplies practical care. <strong>Acts 4:36–37:</strong> Barnabas the Levite gives material support. <strong>Acts 9:26–27:</strong> Barnabas advocates for Saul. <strong>Acts 11:25–26:</strong> Barnabas seeks him and they work together. <strong>Ecclesiastes 4:9–10:</strong> the second person helps when one falls.</p><p>The authored 101 Barnabas Interventions registry and complete book manuscript require separate source-preserving import; this page does not invent or claim to contain those records.</p></section>
<footer>ONE / TABOR ROOT · Authored project remains separate from A vs I gameplay. Public page contains only the introductory creative framework; unpublished original manuscripts are not automatically published.</footer>
</main><script>(function(){'use strict';var k='one.barnabas.localdraft.v1',e=document.getElementById('draft'),s=document.getElementById('status');try{e.value=localStorage.getItem(k)||''}catch(x){s.textContent='Local storage unavailable; use Export.'}document.getElementById('save').addEventListener('click',function(){try{localStorage.setItem(k,e.value);s.textContent='Saved locally. Export a separate backup.'}catch(x){s.textContent='Storage unavailable. Export your draft.'}});document.getElementById('clear').addEventListener('click',function(){if(confirm('Clear the editor? Export any unsaved text first.')){e.value='';s.textContent='Editor cleared. Prior saved draft is unchanged until Save.'}});document.getElementById('export').addEventListener('click',function(){var txt='# Helplessness & Barnabas\nBy Nathan Tabor\n\n'+e.value;var a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([txt],{type:'text/markdown;charset=utf-8'}));a.download='helplessness-barnabas-author-draft.md';a.click();setTimeout(function(){URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href)},2000);s.textContent='Text export started.'})})();</script></body></html>